From: Michael C. Ferguson <michael.christopher.ferguson@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sdhci-cadence: assert the resets before releasing them in probe

sdhci_cdns_probe() only deasserts the controller's resets. On Agilex 5
those are COMBOPHY, SDMMC_OCP and SDMMC (socfpga_agilex5-u-boot.dtsi).
When an earlier stage has already used the controller, for example an
SPL that loaded u-boot.itb from SD, releasing a reset that is already
released does nothing. U-Boot proper then starts from whatever state
that stage left in the host and PHY.

Pulse the resets instead: assert, wait 10 us, deassert. The vendor tree
(Terasic u-boot-socfpga de25-nano-v2025.01) asserts and deasserts the
SDMMC reset in the same place. Nothing changes for a controller that
starts out in reset, or for a board without a resets property.

Upstream status: not submitted yet. Local carry for board/mister/de25nano
(issue #318); see docs/de25-uboot.md section 8.

Signed-off-by: Michael C. Ferguson <michael.christopher.ferguson@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/mmc/sdhci-cadence.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/sdhci-cadence.c
@@ -259,9 +259,14 @@
 	if (!plat->hrs_addr)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
+	/* Pulse rather than only release: a previous stage (e.g. SPL) may have
+	 * left the controller and its PHY configured. */
 	ret = reset_get_bulk(dev, &reset_bulk);
-	if (!ret)
+	if (!ret) {
+		reset_assert_bulk(&reset_bulk);
+		udelay(10);
 		reset_deassert_bulk(&reset_bulk);
+	}
 
 	host->name = dev->name;
 	host->ioaddr = plat->hrs_addr + SDHCI_CDNS_SRS_BASE;
